==Trivia==
*"TzKal" in the [[TzHaar]] language translates into "Champion of the Fire".
*Although TzKal-Zuk is referred to as "him" when it becomes enraged by [[TzHaar-Ket-Keh]], [[Jal-Nib-Rek]] mentions "Zuk is mum".
*TzKal-Zuk is one of the first pieces of content conceived in ''Old School RuneScape'' that went on to be used in ''RuneScape 3''. {{RSL|TzKal-Zuk}} is a demigod warlord from the {{RSL|Second Age}} who acts as {{RSL|Ful|Ful's}} general in the {{RSL|Elder God Wars Dungeon}}.
** The ''RuneScape 3'' variant of Zuk uses a full humanoid model (with feet) and primarily attacks with a {{RSL|Ek-ZekKil|massive obsidian sword}}, though he is also capable of using magic attacks; he is not capable of using ranged attacks. None of his auto-attacks are able to kill the player in a single hit, though he has mechanics which do.
** The ''RuneScape 3'' variant also has a combat level of 14,000, ten times that of the ''Old School RuneScape'' variant.
*Previously, TzKal-Zuk was described by [[TzHaar-Ket-Keh]] as being one of the many newly-hatched feral TzHaar that rose to dominance over its brethren. This no longer appears to be true, and Keh now states that he doesn't know where TzKal-Zuk came from. This change was likely done to keep TzKal-Zuk's lore in ''Old School RuneScape'' consistent with his backstory in ''RuneScape 3''.
*TzKal-Zuk had a festive override wearing a [[santa hat]] during the [[2020 Christmas event/Gallery|2020]], [[2021 Christmas event/Gallery|2021]], [[2022 Christmas event/Gallery|2022]], [[2023 Christmas event/Gallery|2023]], [[2024 Christmas event/Gallery|2024]], and [[2025 Christmas event/Gallery|2025]] Christmas events.
*If you log out and then run out of membership during an Inferno run, you will not lose your slayer task.
*If you log out and then run out of membership and renew on the website before logging back in you will not lose your progress.

